---
description: Data and analytics rules for pipelines, schemas, and privacy
version: 1.0.0
globs: ["data/**", "analytics/**", "etl/**", "apps/**/data/**", "packages/**/data/**", "**/*.sql", "**/*.py", "**/*.ipynb", "**/*.dbt", "**/*.yaml", "**/*.yml"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Treat schemas as contracts; version changes and keep docs/examples current.
- Validate inputs at ingestion; drop or quarantine malformed records with traceable reasons.
- Make transformations deterministic and idempotent; avoid time-dependent surprises.
- Protect PII by default: minimize fields, mask logs, and restrict access paths.
- Track data lineage and ownership; document SLAs and freshness for critical tables.
- Test pipelines (unit for transforms, integration for end-to-end) and add data-quality checks.
- Optimize queries for cost and performance; prefer partition/pruning and avoid SELECT * in prod paths.
- Plan rollouts with backfills or dual-writing where needed; monitor for drift after deploys.
